    "title": "Route-Level State Ownership & Transitions",
    "overviewMetaphor": "The State Lifespan Taxonomy: Where does state live across page transitions? In this architecture, the route parameter (e.g. :projectId) is the authoritative identifier for the current resource, subject to existence, validation, and authorization checks. We classify state into 5 lifespans: Transient View State, Route Parameter State, Ancestor Layout State, Normalized Client State, and Remote/Server Data.",
