    "overviewMetaphor": "Testing a distributed commerce system is like certifying an aerospace vehicle: running thousands of wind-tunnel simulations on isolated airfoils in memory (Unit Tests) costs pennies and runs in milliseconds; verifying the fuel line seals bolted to the real propulsion tank (Integration Tests) costs more but prevents catastrophic propellant leaks; while flying the fully assembled rocket on the launchpad (E2E Tests) is the slowest and most expensive check, reserved strictly to verify final holistic aerodynamics rather than routine valve calibration.",
