          "type": "choose_answer",
          "question": "A regression appeared somewhere between known good tag `v1.0` and bad `HEAD` across 1,024 commits. If a developer uses `git bisect run ./test.sh`, what is the maximum number of test executions required to pinpoint the culprit commit under linear candidate history?",
