        "media": [
          {
            "type": "runnable_code",
            "filename": "day-114-b3_sim.js",
            "initialCode": "// Simulation: Categorized Retry Policy for LLM Integration\nfunction handleLLMError(error, attempt, maxAttempts = 3) {\n  if (error.statusCode === 429 || error.statusCode >= 500) {\n    if (attempt >= maxAttempts) {\n      return { action: 'FAIL_EXHAUSTED', reason: 'Transient error budget exceeded' };\n    }\n    const delay = Math.random() * (100 * Math.pow(2, attempt));\n    return { action: 'RETRY_TRANSIENT', delayMs: Math.round(delay) };\n  }\n  if (error.type === 'VALIDATION_FAILED') {\n    return { action: 'TRIGGER_REPAIR_PROMPT', feedback: error.details };\n  }\n  return { action: 'FAIL_UNRECOVERABLE', reason: 'Non-retryable client error' };\n}"
          }
        ],
        "content": "### Engineering Resilient LLM Workflows\nBuilding production-grade AI features requires treating LLM API calls with the same error discipline applied to external payment gateways or databases:\n\n#### 1. Token Accounting and Truncation\nEvery LLM call consumes two distinct types of tokens: Prompt Tokens (input context) and Completion Tokens (generated output). If your prompt approaches the model context window ceiling, the provider will either reject the request with HTTP 400 or silently truncate early messages. Applications must count prompt tokens locally (via tokenizers like tiktoken) before dispatching requests.\n\n#### 2. Categorized Error Handling\n- **Transient Failures (HTTP 429, 500, 503):** Apply bounded exponential backoff with full jitter and a strict retry budget (e.g. max 3 attempts).\n- **Validation Failures (Malformed Output):** Do NOT blindly resend the identical prompt. Append a structured correction message: *\"Your previous response failed validation with error: [ZodError]. Please regenerate adhering strictly to the schema.\"*\n- **Budget Exhaustion:** If rate limits or repair attempts exceed budget, fail gracefully by serving cached responses, degraded heuristics, or user-facing error notifications.",
