        "content": "### Representing Meaning as Numbers\nTraditional full-text search (lexical search using B-Trees or GIN indexes with tsvector) matches literal words and stems. If a user searches for *\"automobile repair\"*, lexical search misses documents that say *\"fixing cars\"* unless explicit synonym dictionaries exist.\n\n#### Dense Semantic Embeddings\nEmbedding models transform unstructured text strings into fixed-length arrays of floating-point numbers (e.g. 1,536 dimensions in OpenAI text-embedding-3-small, or 768 dimensions in standard BERT models). These dense vectors capture syntactic, stylistic, and semantic relationships learned during training.\n\n#### The Embedding Incompatibility Invariant\nEmbeddings generated by different models should not be assumed to share a compatible semantic space merely because their dimensions match. Vector operations require compatible dimensionality, and cross-model similarity requires an explicitly validated alignment strategy. You cannot compare an embedding from Model A with an embedding from Model B—their internal coordinate systems are completely distinct.",
