    "overviewMetaphor": "Chaos engineering is an earthquake stress test on an aerospace suspension bridge: engineers do not test gentle spring breezes on calm sunny afternoons; they detonate synthetic shock charges under multiple support towers simultaneously (concurrent database failover, cache crash, and upstream gateway timeout) to prove that the bridge flexes within classified deflection bounds rather than shattering into the canyon below.",
